WEBVTT

00:02.336 --> 00:04.589
<i>♪ it seems today
 that all you see ♪</i>

00:04.675 --> 00:07.680
<i>♪ is violence in movies
 and sex on tv ♪</i>

00:07.807 --> 00:11.354
<i>♪ but where are those
 good old-fashioned values ♪</i>

00:11.440 --> 00:14.361
<i>♪ on which we used to rely? ♪</i>

00:14.447 --> 00:17.994
<i>♪ lucky there's a family guy ♪</i>

00:18.079 --> 00:21.293
<i>♪ lucky there's a man who
 positively can do ♪</i>

00:21.420 --> 00:22.921
<i>♪ all the things that make us ♪</i>

00:23.007 --> 00:24.175
<i>♪ laugh and cry ♪</i>

00:24.302 --> 00:30.188
<i>♪ he's... A...
 Fam... Ily... Guy! ♪</i>

00:35.535 --> 00:38.916
Anybody know how to empty
the reservoir on a realdoll?

00:39.001 --> 00:41.421
'cause the website is
mostly testimonials.

00:41.507 --> 00:44.303
Peter, of course you know
what today is.

00:44.388 --> 00:46.641
Yeah, donald sutherland's
birthday.

00:46.769 --> 00:48.854
And maybe another special day?

00:48.940 --> 00:50.274
National dachshund day.

00:50.401 --> 00:54.158
Oh, peter, you forgot our
anniversary again, didn't you?

00:54.285 --> 00:56.956
What? No, no, I-I got you
an awesome gift.

00:57.041 --> 00:58.961
But you can't see it
until tonight.

00:59.046 --> 01:00.548
Tonight? Wh-why tonight?

01:00.675 --> 01:03.387
Oh, you'll see.
Tonight is gonna be amazing.

01:03.472 --> 01:05.141
You're gonna smile
bigger than I did

01:05.226 --> 01:07.354
<i>When I was on the cover
of mad magazine.</i>

01:07.439 --> 01:08.983
[laughs]

01:09.068 --> 01:11.655
<i>You kids don't remember mad
or magazines.</i>

01:11.782 --> 01:14.370
Fortunately, I'm on
broadcast television.

01:14.455 --> 01:16.082
What, me worry?

01:16.209 --> 01:18.086
<i> Okay, me worry.</i>

01:20.677 --> 01:23.265
I wonder how old
donald sutherland is today.

01:23.350 --> 01:25.519
-I don't know, pretty old.
-He looks good, though.

01:25.605 --> 01:27.106
And you know what?
I think the key there

01:27.233 --> 01:28.610
Is never looking good.

01:28.737 --> 01:30.656
Brian, quick, check out
your six o'clock.

01:30.742 --> 01:33.329
Or-or your nine o'clock.
I can't tell time.

01:34.374 --> 01:36.336
A perfectly good mini fridge.

01:36.379 --> 01:38.256
Well, you're gonna have to
fight danny devito for it.

01:38.342 --> 01:39.885
Would you look at that.

01:39.970 --> 01:42.724
A perfectly good,
normal-size fridge.

01:42.810 --> 01:43.977
You know what?

01:44.063 --> 01:46.274
If this works,
I'm going to put it in my room.

01:46.360 --> 01:48.403
Stewie, you're too little
to have a fridge in your room.

01:48.490 --> 01:50.617
Think whatever you want, brian,
but I'm taking this

01:50.786 --> 01:51.995
Before danny devito gets it.

01:52.039 --> 01:54.251
That's all right, kid.
I don't need it anymore.

01:54.378 --> 01:56.129
<i>[singers]
♪ danny devito ♪</i>

01:56.257 --> 01:58.718
<i>♪ got bit by a magic mosquito. ♪</i>

01:58.804 --> 02:01.140
[announcer] danny devito
and the magic mosquito,

02:01.309 --> 02:02.936
<i> Now streaming on peacock.</i>

02:03.064 --> 02:05.734
I'm hearing a lot of buzz.

02:09.536 --> 02:12.499
There he is.
Here comes the groom!

02:12.584 --> 02:14.044
-[noisemakers blare]
-[applause]

02:14.171 --> 02:16.383
Geez, even you guys know
it's my anniversary?

02:16.427 --> 02:18.178
-How is that possible?
-It's easy.

02:18.306 --> 02:20.767
-I follow your wife.
-You mean on instagram?

02:21.772 --> 02:22.731
Yep.

02:22.816 --> 02:24.234
Peter, let me guess.

02:24.361 --> 02:26.196
You forgot
your anniversary again.

02:26.240 --> 02:28.577
Yeah. What's worse, I lied,
and I told lois

02:28.746 --> 02:30.456
I had a awesome gift planned
for tonight.

02:30.624 --> 02:32.168
If I don't come up with
something amazing,

02:32.295 --> 02:33.463
I am so screwed.

02:33.590 --> 02:35.760
Hey, you want to
give lois a treat?

02:35.887 --> 02:36.970
Popcorn-ucopia.

02:37.056 --> 02:38.474
Now, they're a little outfit
out there

02:38.601 --> 02:41.063
In fort wayne, indiana,
family owned and operated

02:41.148 --> 02:44.403
For five generations over there
in the "crossroads of america."

02:44.489 --> 02:45.615
Indiana's state motto.

02:45.700 --> 02:47.452
And get this.
They make a metal cannister

02:47.537 --> 02:49.373
With three different kinds
of popcorn,

02:49.459 --> 02:51.211
But they're separated!

02:51.338 --> 02:53.841
Maybe you should just
take lois out

02:53.927 --> 02:55.387
To a fine restaurant.

02:55.472 --> 02:58.852
Now, I can hear some of you
saying, "joe, why separated?"

02:58.979 --> 03:00.731
None of us are saying that, joe.

03:00.818 --> 03:02.151
Okay, here's why.

03:02.278 --> 03:05.117
Three flavors of popcorn
in one tin, and they don't mix.

03:05.244 --> 03:06.787
Unless, of course,
you want them to mix.

03:06.914 --> 03:08.081
This is a home run, man.

03:08.167 --> 03:09.584
Kind of short notice
to get a good table

03:09.711 --> 03:10.921
In any restaurant.

03:11.048 --> 03:12.633
I don't think you appreciate
that they don't mix.

03:12.760 --> 03:14.638
Your caramel corn stays separate
from your cheese corn,

03:14.765 --> 03:16.224
Which stays separate
from your corn corn.

03:16.310 --> 03:18.020
You see, in the past,
you would need

03:18.106 --> 03:19.858
-Three tubs of corn.
-Yes, we get it!

03:19.985 --> 03:21.528
We know about the corn, joe!

03:21.655 --> 03:24.493
[chuckles]
honestly, I don't think you do.

03:24.579 --> 03:26.289
Forgive me for eavesdropping,

03:26.416 --> 03:29.086
But I have a flat-bottom dory
with a quiet outboard

03:29.205 --> 03:30.423
I'd be glad to lend you.

03:30.550 --> 03:32.427
Full moon tonight.
Why not take your bride

03:32.513 --> 03:35.142
On a romantic cruise
around quahog harbor?

03:35.227 --> 03:37.388
You know what?
I think lois would like that.

03:37.441 --> 03:40.654
Ooh, the romantic boat ride
is the perfect surprise.

03:40.740 --> 03:42.283
You can bring along
a tub of popcorn,

03:42.368 --> 03:43.285
'cause the tin's waterproof.

03:43.370 --> 03:44.662
And if you'd like, I could also

03:44.832 --> 03:48.046
Row up alongside you and
play "brandy" on the accordion.

03:48.173 --> 03:49.465
Yeah, no, just the boat, thanks.

03:49.550 --> 03:51.512
Aw, I always drive past my exit.

03:51.639 --> 03:53.182
Lois is gonna love this, peter.

03:53.226 --> 03:54.519
She's gonna think
you're a true romantic,

03:54.646 --> 03:55.896
Like michael douglas.

03:55.981 --> 03:59.905
So who wants to hear
how I think I got mouth cancer?

04:01.828 --> 04:02.954
She's, uh...

04:03.039 --> 04:04.749
She's heard this one before.

04:07.550 --> 04:08.800
Check it out, rupert.

04:08.885 --> 04:10.345
Juice box, boom!

04:10.430 --> 04:11.557
Go-gurts? Yep.

04:11.642 --> 04:13.394
And most importantly,
for freshness,

04:13.479 --> 04:16.191
An open box of
armie hammer's baking powder,

04:16.318 --> 04:18.613
Now with 40% more fingers.

04:18.740 --> 04:21.662
Pretty much all he had to do
was not eat people.

04:21.747 --> 04:23.374
How the hell did you
get that up here?

04:23.459 --> 04:25.211
With no help from you, thanks.

04:25.339 --> 04:27.341
But you know what?
You still get a cola.

04:27.468 --> 04:29.430
Ah. Convenient, I guess.

04:29.557 --> 04:30.765
Can's not so cold, though.

04:30.851 --> 04:32.770
Yeah, everything in there
is either lukewarm

04:32.897 --> 04:34.189
Or frozen solid.

04:34.233 --> 04:35.610
Stewie, I still think
it's a bad idea

04:35.737 --> 04:36.988
For you to have this thing
in here.

04:37.073 --> 04:38.900
Yeah, not really looking for
advice from the guy

04:38.910 --> 04:42.500
Who puts a fire emoji on
all dua lipa's instagram posts.

04:42.628 --> 04:44.129
She's not gonna respond, bri.

04:44.256 --> 04:46.342
She used to respond
before she had so many fans.

04:46.470 --> 04:48.639
She was 14!
And she thought you were 11

04:48.724 --> 04:51.019
-Because you said you were 11.
-Because I was 11!

04:51.104 --> 04:52.773
See? You're still saying it.

04:55.573 --> 04:57.742
Well, happy anniversary, lois.

04:57.827 --> 05:00.081
Huh? Did I tell you?
Isn't this nice?

05:00.208 --> 05:02.586
You know, I have to admit
I had my doubts,

05:02.672 --> 05:05.385
But you really surprised me.

05:05.428 --> 05:07.514
A romantic dinner on a boat?

05:07.642 --> 05:09.519
Right? Who needs
a fancy restaurant

05:09.646 --> 05:11.523
When you can be wet
and kind of dizzy?

05:11.608 --> 05:14.028
Oh, peter, it's just perfect.

05:14.115 --> 05:15.365
Well, except for
that cruise ship

05:15.492 --> 05:17.327
That still can't dock
because of covid.

05:17.414 --> 05:19.207
Is the election over yet?

05:19.292 --> 05:21.546
We are all pooping in the sink!

05:21.673 --> 05:24.176
I'm from iowa, so I still think
this is awesome.

05:24.303 --> 05:26.139
Oh, there's something
about the ocean

05:26.266 --> 05:28.644
That's always been
so magical to me.

05:28.730 --> 05:31.901
And I say we celebrate.

05:32.029 --> 05:33.405
[gasps]

05:36.957 --> 05:38.876
Ah, now we're talking.

05:38.961 --> 05:41.758
All right, cannonball!

05:46.019 --> 05:47.896
<i>[voice muffled]
♪ there's got to be ♪</i>

05:47.981 --> 05:51.153
<i>♪ a morning after. ♪</i>

05:51.238 --> 05:52.782
[people scream]

05:54.037 --> 05:55.955
[lois laughs]

05:56.082 --> 05:58.252
Peter, I feel like a kid again.

05:58.338 --> 06:00.048
Isn't this exhilarating?

06:00.133 --> 06:01.968
The moon, the stars,

06:02.096 --> 06:04.725
The dark triangular
dorsal fin heading our way.

06:04.852 --> 06:08.525
The dark triangular dorsal fin
heading our way!

06:10.072 --> 06:11.073
Shark!

06:11.200 --> 06:12.827
[panicked shouts]

06:14.833 --> 06:16.668
[lois cries out]

06:18.048 --> 06:21.930
Peter! Peter, don't leave me
to die out here!

06:22.057 --> 06:24.018
Peter, come back!

06:24.104 --> 06:27.359
Hold on, lois. I'm gonna grab
a real quick hot chocolate.

06:27.444 --> 06:28.946
Warm up my bones.

06:31.327 --> 06:32.495
[screams]

06:32.622 --> 06:34.457
-[screams]
-[squeaking]

06:34.586 --> 06:36.796
Oh, god. Thank god.

06:36.965 --> 06:38.676
It's just a dolphin.

06:40.139 --> 06:41.390
[grunts]

06:41.517 --> 06:43.227
[panting]

06:43.313 --> 06:44.731
Ah, perfect.

06:49.159 --> 06:50.201
[phone dings]

06:58.680 --> 07:00.808
Hey, good morning, lovebirds.

07:00.936 --> 07:02.687
So, how'd
the moonlight cruise go?

07:02.814 --> 07:05.193
Dad saw a shark
and left mom to die.

07:05.362 --> 07:06.821
Oh, come on.
All that nice stuff

07:06.907 --> 07:09.703
I did last night, we're only
gonna focus on that one thing?

07:09.830 --> 07:11.248
Damn it, peter,
you're supposed to be

07:11.334 --> 07:12.626
The alpha in my life.

07:12.711 --> 07:14.881
Someone to stand up
and take charge.

07:14.967 --> 07:17.972
But you never even looked back
to see if I was okay.

07:18.057 --> 07:19.809
Y-you just raced off.

07:19.894 --> 07:22.147
You hear about anne heche?
Sad, huh?

07:22.233 --> 07:23.818
Peter, don't try
to change the subject!

07:23.945 --> 07:25.613
You were always jealous of her!

07:25.782 --> 07:26.825
You know what, peter?

07:26.910 --> 07:28.662
I am so disappointed in you,

07:28.747 --> 07:31.292
I am taking the exclamation
points out of this argument.

07:31.378 --> 07:32.504
You can't do that.

07:32.631 --> 07:34.675
Male arguments are powerless
without volume.

07:34.761 --> 07:36.638
That just leaves us with words.

07:37.434 --> 07:38.726
[calmly]
I'm done here.

07:40.858 --> 07:43.696
Wow, peter, I've never
seen lois so upset.

07:43.823 --> 07:44.823
Looks like you're in--

07:44.908 --> 07:46.452
And I find this phrase
offensive--

07:46.579 --> 07:47.704
The doghouse.

07:47.832 --> 07:49.992
Oh, I've solved
bigger problems than this.

07:50.045 --> 07:52.548
Like when I forgot the safe word
at that sex party.

07:52.676 --> 07:54.511
Aardvark. Aah!

07:54.555 --> 07:56.599
Aardwolf. Abacus. Aah!

07:56.684 --> 07:59.189
Abandon. Aah! Abase. Aah!

07:59.274 --> 08:01.568
Abate. Aah! Abattoir.

08:01.654 --> 08:03.364
<i>[peter]
 the good news was
 I had memorized</i>

08:03.450 --> 08:05.870
<i> The entire dictionary
 when I got bored over covid.</i>

08:05.955 --> 08:08.334
<i> The bad news was
 the safe word was "zyzzyva,"</i>

08:08.461 --> 08:10.129
<i> A genus of
 south american weevils,</i>

08:10.256 --> 08:13.095
<i> Which, coincidentally,
 I was forced to keister.</i>

08:13.138 --> 08:16.059
[reggae music playing]

08:17.314 --> 08:19.358
[phone clicking]

08:22.910 --> 08:25.247
Bri, what up, dawg?
Grab a brewski from the mini.

08:25.332 --> 08:26.415
I can't have any more, though.

08:26.459 --> 08:28.044
Got to cram for a test
in the morning.

08:28.171 --> 08:30.216
Where exactly
are you going to school?

08:30.301 --> 08:32.262
Um, university of college.

08:32.347 --> 08:33.515
Not for long, though.

08:33.600 --> 08:35.644
Just got my grades. Not good.

08:35.772 --> 08:36.772
Stewie, I think
this fridge thing...

08:36.941 --> 08:38.609
<i>Yo check out my maxim posters.</i>

08:38.736 --> 08:41.616
Hot, right? No, no. Yes, yes.

08:41.743 --> 08:43.162
No, yes, no.

08:43.330 --> 08:46.502
-Why would you put up the nos?
-So you know when it's a yes.

08:46.629 --> 08:47.964
Stewie, we got to talk.

08:48.091 --> 08:50.010
Brah, if this is about
you and I being roommates,

08:50.095 --> 08:52.140
I was gonna put a word in
with colin,

08:52.184 --> 08:53.142
But I already have one.

08:53.269 --> 08:55.230
Brian, meet guy.

08:55.316 --> 08:57.526
Guy? Okay. Pleased to meet you.

08:57.653 --> 08:58.946
Oh, guy doesn't speak
much english.

08:59.073 --> 09:00.951
He's from quebec.
Engineering, I think.

09:01.078 --> 09:04.041
But he is insane, brian.
A legend.

09:04.126 --> 09:05.837
<i>Guy. Allons.</i>

09:08.637 --> 09:10.388
Ah, look at him drinking
that soda.

09:10.474 --> 09:11.683
Classic guy.

09:11.810 --> 09:13.646
-Okay, anyway, stewie...
-Can't talk now, bri.

09:13.773 --> 09:16.402
Got to spend some time
messing around on the guitar.

09:16.529 --> 09:19.533
[discordant notes]

09:19.620 --> 09:20.870
I didn't even know you played.

09:20.997 --> 09:22.624
Oh, yeah, all the time. A lot.

09:22.709 --> 09:24.587
Bros down the hall
call me "ramen,"

09:24.673 --> 09:25.547
'cause I'm always noodling.

09:25.633 --> 09:28.011
Hey, what's going on, no pubes?

09:28.097 --> 09:31.227
They-they... They call,
they call me a lot of things.

09:33.651 --> 09:35.988
Lois, I told you
I would make it up to you,

09:36.115 --> 09:38.576
So I got you something
very special.

09:38.662 --> 09:41.959
<i>I got you in the opening credits
of snl.</i>

09:42.044 --> 09:43.296
<i>-[lively music playing]
-[peter] okay, look.</i>

09:43.381 --> 09:44.882
<i> Here comes kenan.</i>

09:45.010 --> 09:46.845
<i> Oh, look at him
 playfully hailing a cab.</i>

09:48.267 --> 09:49.559
<i> And here you are.</i>

09:49.686 --> 09:51.062
<i> Look how cool and hip you look</i>

09:51.231 --> 09:54.028
<i> Walking by a manhole cover
 with steam coming out of it.</i>

09:55.533 --> 09:58.412
<i> Uhp, looks like kenan's
still trying to wave down a cab.</i>

09:58.497 --> 10:02.087
<i> Ah, there you go again!
 Now you're at the club,</i>

10:02.173 --> 10:04.091
<i> Holding up a "one more" signal
 for a drink.</i>

10:05.430 --> 10:07.223
<i>Why won't nobody stop for kenan?</i>

10:08.395 --> 10:11.316
<i> Oh, but mikey day
 gets a cab first try.</i>

10:11.443 --> 10:12.778
<i>Oh, he's sharing it with kenan.</i>

10:12.905 --> 10:14.448
<i> He's sharing it. Okay.</i>

10:14.575 --> 10:18.832
<i> Oh, a very stressful
 opening credits this week.</i>

10:21.006 --> 10:23.468
Stewie, did you do this?

10:23.553 --> 10:26.015
Geez, brian, don't just come
barging in here like that.

10:26.101 --> 10:28.270
I thought you were
campus security.

10:29.400 --> 10:30.776
Guy pushed an air conditioner

10:30.903 --> 10:32.405
Off the parking garage
yesterday.

10:32.532 --> 10:34.493
Almost hit
a public safety officer.

10:34.620 --> 10:35.787
By the way, that's between us.

10:35.956 --> 10:37.541
They're going door to door.
It's pretty serious.

10:37.669 --> 10:38.710
I don't care about that.

10:38.879 --> 10:40.673
I want to know who wrote
"renob" on my chest

10:40.800 --> 10:41.968
When I was sleeping.

10:42.053 --> 10:44.432
"renob"? Brian,
you read that in the mirror.

10:44.517 --> 10:46.144
-It's "boner."
-what?!

10:46.312 --> 10:47.480
Great. Thanks, bri.

10:47.566 --> 10:49.944
Now we've got the r.A.
Coming in to check on us.

10:50.029 --> 10:52.198
Hey, stewie, guy, look,

10:52.326 --> 10:56.500
I like fun as much as anybody,
but we've had some complaints,

10:56.586 --> 10:59.841
And you really got to keep
the noise down in here.

10:59.926 --> 11:02.890
Oh, and, hey, I reviewed
your party application,

11:02.975 --> 11:04.602
And everything looks
to be in order,

11:04.729 --> 11:06.397
So you're good to go.

11:06.483 --> 11:07.901
Whoa, whoa, whoa,
wait a minute. Party?

11:07.986 --> 11:10.071
-Who's having a party?
-I am.

11:10.241 --> 11:12.577
And it'll be loaded
with chicks, thanks to guy.

11:12.663 --> 11:14.248
This guy's all about
the poutine,

11:14.334 --> 11:16.503
Which sounds dirty,
but it's just a gravy

11:16.588 --> 11:17.881
They put on french fries.

11:17.966 --> 11:20.261
Stewie, you've taken this
mini fridge thing too far.

11:20.388 --> 11:21.806
I'm moving this thing
out of here.

11:21.892 --> 11:23.977
Oh, be careful, bri.
Not a good idea.

11:24.105 --> 11:25.564
You don't want to piss off guy.

11:25.651 --> 11:26.984
Yesterday he crow-hopped
a dip tin

11:27.111 --> 11:28.446
And knocked a guy out.

11:28.532 --> 11:29.573
Oh, wow, did he really?

11:29.701 --> 11:32.079
Well, now I'm so
very scared of guy.

11:32.165 --> 11:34.417
-Aah!
-Oh, ho, ho, guy.

11:34.545 --> 11:36.256
<i> Ce fut un grand lancer!</i>

11:36.341 --> 11:38.426
<i> Je crois qu'il est mort, eh?</i>

11:43.398 --> 11:46.319
Special flowers
for a special lady.

11:46.446 --> 11:47.906
Hmm. These are nice.

11:48.033 --> 11:49.410
Except... [sniffs]

11:49.495 --> 11:51.581
They smell like--
what is that, exhaust?

11:51.624 --> 11:54.546
Why is there a picture
of a teenage latina on them?

11:54.590 --> 11:57.218
Peter, did you steal these
from a roadside memorial?

11:57.304 --> 11:59.640
They didn't love her
as much as I love you, lois.

11:59.768 --> 12:01.604
Besides, it's not like
she can see 'em.

12:01.731 --> 12:03.859
Stolen flowers? Really, peter?

12:03.986 --> 12:05.361
Is that all I mean to you?

12:05.405 --> 12:07.073
Well, there's also a candle
with one of them

12:07.201 --> 12:09.078
<i>Spooky skeletons from coco.</i>

12:09.205 --> 12:11.584
You know, peter,
a relationship is

12:11.669 --> 12:13.421
Supposed to grow over time,

12:13.506 --> 12:16.053
To give you a sense of purpose
and meaning.

12:16.138 --> 12:18.015
But after all these years
with you,

12:18.100 --> 12:20.479
I-I just feel worthless.

12:20.564 --> 12:24.028
I feel as worthless as any coin
smaller than a quarter.

12:24.113 --> 12:26.785
Hello, my name is nickel.

12:26.870 --> 12:28.120
[all]
hi, nickel.

12:28.206 --> 12:30.250
There was a time when I paid for

12:30.378 --> 12:32.923
A ride on a trolley,
or a good cigar,

12:32.966 --> 12:35.846
Or a hand-cranked film
of a man tipping his hat

12:35.932 --> 12:37.684
And twirling his moustache.

12:37.769 --> 12:40.857
But yesterday, I was part of
a handful of change

12:40.943 --> 12:42.236
At a mcdonald's,

12:42.321 --> 12:44.448
And the teenage girl
threw us out.

12:44.576 --> 12:48.542
Just-just threw us in the trash
with the wrappers and the bag.

12:48.627 --> 12:50.128
[sobs]

12:50.256 --> 12:52.007
Yeah. And I'm voiced
by kevin hart.

12:52.135 --> 12:54.763
<i>[announcer] coming this fall
 from pixar, coins!</i>

12:54.849 --> 12:58.271
<i> We'll keep making things talk
 until you don't show up.</i>

12:58.357 --> 13:00.359
Come on, lois. Are you gonna
stay mad at me forever?

13:00.445 --> 13:03.115
I've done stupid things before,
and you've always forgiven me.

13:03.243 --> 13:04.870
Oh, I forgive you, peter.

13:04.997 --> 13:06.707
I just don't think
I'll ever be able to see you

13:06.834 --> 13:10.339
As a man, my protector
or a real husband again.

13:10.467 --> 13:12.261
Oh, okay.

13:12.346 --> 13:13.638
I see.

13:13.808 --> 13:16.479
Well, if that's how you feel,
I'll just take my things

13:16.564 --> 13:17.940
And get out of your way.

13:21.283 --> 13:23.160
This is a different realdoll.

13:23.245 --> 13:25.415
I never figured out
how to empty the other one.

13:31.640 --> 13:32.973
This is not good, guys.

13:33.059 --> 13:34.393
She put a little
black-and-white tv

13:34.521 --> 13:36.982
On the sun porch
and then slept there last night.

13:37.068 --> 13:40.281
Ooh, that's the angriest
a new England wife can get.

13:40.367 --> 13:42.787
Look, if I could do it
all over again, I'd save her,

13:42.872 --> 13:44.249
'cause now I know
it was a dolphin

13:44.376 --> 13:45.919
And there was no real danger.

13:46.046 --> 13:47.046
Peter, don't you see?

13:47.174 --> 13:49.009
We got to make you
the hero again.

13:49.053 --> 13:50.136
Wait, say that again.

13:50.264 --> 13:52.308
We got to make you
the hero again.

13:52.435 --> 13:53.728
Yep, yeah, you got weird teeth.

13:53.856 --> 13:56.609
Wait. What did you say before
about the hero thing?

13:56.695 --> 13:58.405
I said we've got to make peter
the hero...

13:58.491 --> 14:00.201
You're right.
He does have weird teeth.

14:00.328 --> 14:03.207
I just have to show lois
I can still be her hero.

14:03.293 --> 14:05.170
[muffled]
that's exactly
what I was saying.

14:05.256 --> 14:08.303
[loud dance music playing]

14:13.190 --> 14:15.192
Brian, you made it.

14:15.278 --> 14:18.033
Aw, damn it,
I love this son of a bitch.

14:18.118 --> 14:19.953
Are you... Are you drunk?

14:20.039 --> 14:21.999
Nah, I just spun around
a few times.

14:22.085 --> 14:24.129
Stewie, it's-it's really loud.

14:24.214 --> 14:25.466
Oh, that's all guy, man.

14:25.593 --> 14:28.055
His speakers aren't even
legal in america.

14:28.098 --> 14:30.393
Stewie, you were supposed to be
in bed at 7:50.

14:30.520 --> 14:33.484
The only clock we have in here
says "miller time."

14:33.611 --> 14:35.738
Come on, brian, this could be
the greatest night of our lives,

14:35.866 --> 14:38.995
But you're all, "stewie's too
little to have a mini fridge."

14:39.081 --> 14:41.042
What happened to the brian
I used to know?

14:41.127 --> 14:42.796
[dance music continues louder]

14:47.684 --> 14:49.143
You know what? You're right.

14:49.270 --> 14:50.689
I guess I was just worried
about your safety.

14:50.816 --> 14:51.899
But what the hell.

14:52.068 --> 14:53.821
I can party with
the best of them, even guy.

14:53.906 --> 14:55.156
There you go.

14:55.325 --> 14:57.537
What's the worst that could
happen, right? Check it.

14:57.622 --> 14:59.374
Guy put his speakers
out the window,

14:59.460 --> 15:01.003
And he's cranking wagner.

15:01.131 --> 15:03.008
Everybody's like, "what?!"

15:03.093 --> 15:05.847
["ride of the valkyries"
playing over speakers]

15:05.933 --> 15:08.144
♪ ♪

15:17.291 --> 15:19.377
You know, I don't know why
I let you talk me into

15:19.463 --> 15:20.630
Coming back down here.

15:20.758 --> 15:23.636
Because in your heart,
you know I love you, lois.

15:23.680 --> 15:25.850
And because,
as chris daughtry says,

15:25.977 --> 15:27.854
I'll try to do it right
this time.

15:27.940 --> 15:29.107
It's not over.

15:29.234 --> 15:31.279
-Hmm. Daughtry says it better.
-I agree.

15:31.364 --> 15:33.366
<i>-[phone beeps]
 -hi, lois.</i>

15:33.452 --> 15:35.330
<i> Your husband peter
 wanted me to tell you</i>

15:35.415 --> 15:37.835
<i> He'll try to do it right
 this time, and...</i>

15:37.921 --> 15:41.093
<i>♪ it's not over. ♪</i>

15:41.136 --> 15:44.350
<i>Also, you may want to remind him
 that his venmo did not work,</i>

15:44.435 --> 15:47.774
<i> And we're gonna need to find
an alternative form of payment.</i>

15:47.901 --> 15:48.943
[gasps]

15:49.029 --> 15:50.989
Oh, if he was wearing
that straw hat,

15:51.075 --> 15:52.785
I would've wet myself.

15:52.870 --> 15:54.957
♪ ♪

15:55.042 --> 15:56.961
Oh, he's got her. [laughs]

15:57.046 --> 15:59.508
The daughtry thing worked,
quagmire.

15:59.636 --> 16:00.928
Of course it did.

16:01.013 --> 16:04.645
Sometimes I suffer under
the weight of my own genius.

16:05.524 --> 16:06.691
We're all set.

16:06.776 --> 16:08.946
This is gonna work
as long as peter remembers

16:09.073 --> 16:11.577
To have lois
step on the 18th plank.

16:12.414 --> 16:14.207
18th plank. 18th plank.

16:14.335 --> 16:15.711
Eighteen. Eighteen.

16:15.796 --> 16:17.381
Oh, I wonder if
daughtry's coming to

16:17.466 --> 16:19.511
The quahog amphitheater
this season.

16:19.597 --> 16:23.729
Let's see, blink-182,
twenty one pilots,

16:23.856 --> 16:25.775
Thirty seconds to mars...

16:25.861 --> 16:27.821
182, 21, 30.

16:27.948 --> 16:29.116
10,000 maniacs?

16:29.243 --> 16:31.872
Geez, how old is
natalie merchant now? 60?

16:31.999 --> 16:33.459
10,000, 60.

16:33.586 --> 16:35.589
Look, lois, I'll take you
to every one of those shows

16:35.707 --> 16:38.136
If you just stop saying numbers
and get on the damn pier.

16:38.222 --> 16:41.644
Uh, I-I mean,
after you, my queen.

16:43.901 --> 16:45.653
♪ ♪

16:57.055 --> 16:58.933
Uh, no, no. Wrong plank.
Not there.

16:59.018 --> 17:00.302
-Huh?
-No, it's nothing.

17:00.396 --> 17:02.022
I just think you were
supposed to step here.

17:02.149 --> 17:03.567
[grunts]

17:07.035 --> 17:09.289
What the hell?
Peter, are you okay?

17:09.416 --> 17:10.834
Uh, don't worry, lois.

17:10.961 --> 17:13.632
I'll protect you
if there's any sharks around.

17:14.678 --> 17:17.557
I said, if there's
any sharks around.

17:17.643 --> 17:19.687
Peter, I'm not ready.
I lost one of my flippers.

17:19.772 --> 17:21.190
What do you mean,
you're not ready?

17:21.276 --> 17:22.443
It's not gonna work
without a shark.

17:22.571 --> 17:24.364
Oh, don't worry,
there's one right there.

17:25.744 --> 17:27.997
♪ ♪

17:28.082 --> 17:29.292
Oh, phew.

17:29.419 --> 17:30.754
[screaming]

17:40.109 --> 17:41.361
[farts]

17:41.863 --> 17:44.576
[screaming]

17:53.138 --> 17:55.517
[both screaming]

17:57.189 --> 17:58.899
Thank god.

17:58.984 --> 18:00.111
Peter, are you all right?

18:00.154 --> 18:02.783
Lois, you saved me.

18:03.745 --> 18:05.539
[panting]

18:05.708 --> 18:06.959
[gasps, chokes]

18:09.801 --> 18:12.513
Peter, did you rig
this whole thing

18:12.640 --> 18:14.517
So that I would fall
into the water?

18:14.603 --> 18:16.230
Yes.

18:16.315 --> 18:18.610
I guess now you're
really mad at me, huh?

18:18.696 --> 18:21.158
You know what? I'm not.

18:21.285 --> 18:23.412
Because I just realized
something, peter.

18:23.498 --> 18:25.459
I do have an alpha in my life,

18:25.586 --> 18:29.133
Someone to stand up
and take charge, and it's me.

18:29.261 --> 18:30.544
It's always been me.

18:30.597 --> 18:32.808
And I will never again
look outside of myself

18:32.894 --> 18:35.564
For happiness, validation
or anything.

18:35.692 --> 18:39.072
And you, you helped me
see this, peter. Thank you.

18:39.158 --> 18:40.492
Okay.

18:40.661 --> 18:42.371
And you're sure you're not mad?

18:42.499 --> 18:45.670
Oh, no, peter, I'm not mad.

18:45.756 --> 18:48.635
I'm horny. Hornier than
I've been in a long time.

18:48.721 --> 18:51.850
Now, get those pants off,
you fat little bag of dirt.

18:51.937 --> 18:53.103
Oh.

18:53.189 --> 18:55.526
[growling playfully]

18:55.653 --> 18:56.820
[laughing nervously]

18:56.906 --> 18:58.240
[growling playfully]

18:58.325 --> 18:59.660
Happy anniversary?

18:59.787 --> 19:01.957
I didn't say you could talk!

19:02.042 --> 19:04.337
But happy anniversary, peter.

19:04.464 --> 19:06.466
[moaning]

19:08.932 --> 19:10.643
This is awesome.

19:10.728 --> 19:13.524
You know, for a fat guy,
peter's got a tiny ass.

19:13.651 --> 19:16.447
Perfectly separated popcorn,
anyone?

19:17.702 --> 19:19.453
This is good.
Where'd you get it?

19:19.582 --> 19:21.584
An elder abuse victim
sent it to the station

19:21.669 --> 19:24.882
As a thank-you
for arresting her grandson.

19:24.968 --> 19:27.013
I'm just glad something good
came out of it.

19:34.406 --> 19:37.452
[giggling, moaning]

19:40.502 --> 19:42.964
Don't be late for work,
now, peter.

19:43.050 --> 19:45.763
-Yah!
-Ooh! Ow. Fresh.

19:45.848 --> 19:47.433
See you tonight.

19:47.518 --> 19:49.270
It's good to see you two
getting along.

19:49.356 --> 19:51.107
Oh, yeah. Our marriage
will be just fine

19:51.193 --> 19:53.906
As long as peter remembers
that I am everything

19:54.033 --> 19:55.241
And he is nothing.

19:55.327 --> 19:56.453
Is stewie still sleeping?

19:56.580 --> 19:58.582
Probably. He was up
pretty late last night.

19:58.710 --> 20:00.796
I'll go check on him.

20:00.923 --> 20:02.466
Stewie, you up?

20:02.593 --> 20:03.969
That was some...

20:04.055 --> 20:06.100
♪ ♪

20:11.113 --> 20:12.029
Oh, my god!

20:12.115 --> 20:13.491
Damn it, stewie, I told you

20:13.660 --> 20:15.537
You were too little
to have a fridge in your room.

20:15.622 --> 20:19.212
[sobbing]
oh... Oh, god.

20:19.297 --> 20:21.634
[sobbing continues]

20:21.761 --> 20:24.933
["midnight, the stars and you"
playing]